WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.775
Why does this chapter exist?

2
00:00:01.775 --> 00:00:03.612
Because of one quiet failure.

3
00:00:03.612 --> 00:00:08.137
A federated credential with the wrong
subject is created without any error.

4
00:00:08.137 --> 00:00:12.516
Nothing complains until the day the
workload tries to exchange its token,

5
00:00:12.516 --> 00:00:15.962
and for GitHub, Learn says even
that fails without an error.

6
00:00:15.962 --> 00:00:18.701
The plan's risk register
names exactly this,

7
00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:23.188
and its answer is to test every exchange
before the parallel run starts.

8
00:00:23.188 --> 00:00:25.525
That test is the center of the chapter.

9
00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:28.208
The order of conversion comes from Book 2:

10
00:00:28.208 --> 00:00:32.785
managed identities where the host
is in Azure, federated credentials

11
00:00:32.785 --> 00:00:37.180
where the host speaks O I D C,
certificates only where neither works.
